{"name": "mitosalt", "id": "67c0c7171c95a93990c81078", "package_types": ["conda"], "summary": "MitoSAlt is a pipeline to identify large deletions and duplications in human and mouse mitochondrial genomes from next generation whole genome/exome sequencing data. The pipeline is capable of analyzing any circular genome in principle, as long as a proper configuration file is provided.", "description": "This mitosalt version can:\n\n- download user-selected reference genomes\n  - `download-mitosalt-db.sh -h [human_genome_url, blank for custom hg19 genome]`\n  - `download-mitosalt-db.sh -m [mouse_genome_url, blank for custom GRCm38.p6 genome]`\n  - `download-mitosalt-db.sh -h [human_genome_url, blank for custom hg19 genome] -m [mouse_genome_url, blank for custom GRCm38.p6 genome]`\n- let us choose the destination folder of the reference genomes and indices\n  - `export MITOSALTDATA=/path/to/mitosalt/genomedata`\n- specify custom config files that are available in the package at `$CONDA_PREFIX/share/mitosalt-1.1.1-0/`\n", "home": "https://sourceforge.net/projects/mitosalt/", "public": true, "access": "public", "owner": {"company": "", "location": "", "login": "bioconda", "name": "bioconda", "url": "", "description": "Bioconda is a distribution of bioinformatics software realized as a channel for the versatile Conda package manager.", "created_at": "2015-09-11 22:59:20.880000+00:00", "user_type": "org"}, "full_name": "bioconda/mitosalt", "url": "http://api.anaconda.org/packages/bioconda/mitosalt", "html_url": "http://anaconda.org/bioconda/mitosalt", "versions": ["1.1.1"], "latest_version": "1.1.1", "platforms": {"noarch": "1.1.1"}, "conda_platforms": ["noarch"], "revision": 6, "license": "MIT-0", "license_url": null, "dev_url": null, "doc_url": null, "source_git_url": null, "source_git_tag": null, "app_entry": {}, "app_type": {}, "app_summary": {}, "builds": ["hdfd78af_2", "hdfd78af_1", "hdfd78af_3", "hdfd78af_0"], "ndownloads": 584, "releases": [{"version": "1.1.1", "distr